schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Distributed Leadership
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Leadership where multiple people hold leadership responsibilities and
    power flows contextually, rather than concentrating in one founder or
    "heroic leader."
  source_traditions:
    - >-
      organizing/community-organizing training traditions (cited: "Organizing
      for America training materials")
      cooperative leadership development practice
    - >-
      East African / Somaliland relational-authority traditions (clan
      elders, women's group leaders, mosque committee members, trading
      network coordinators) named explicitly as a cultural foundation to
      build on rather than replace
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Positioned as the resolution to the article's "leadership paradox" —
    not less leadership, but a different kind, distributed across roles and
    people so no single point of failure exists.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - the "founder trap" (single-founder model this concept is defined against)
    - shared/rotating leadership (a specific structural technique, see role rotation)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      distributed leadership ≠ no leadership — the article is explicit that
      "too little leadership and nothing gets done"; the goal is
      distribution, not absence
  tensions:
    - >-
      the article imports Western organizing-training language ("Organizing
      for America") for a technique it then explicitly grounds in existing
      East African/Somaliland relational authority — worth watching whether
      the framing privileges the imported vocabulary over the local one
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    "Distributed leadership" as a slogan can mask real power concentration
    if roles are distributed on paper but one person retains informal veto
    — the article's own "Mistake 4: Concentrating Power" section names this
    risk directly.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/leadership-development.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
